WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:43.271
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.541 --> 00:45.291
Four Weasels down.

3
00:58.458 --> 00:59.625
Hawk, Alpha One.

4
01:00.916 --> 01:03.041
Alpha team has arrived.

5
01:18.541 --> 01:19.583
Hostages.

6
01:21.041 --> 01:22.750
Hawk, Alpha One.

7
01:23.416 --> 01:24.541
Alpha One, come in.

8
01:25.291 --> 01:27.041
We found two hostages.

9
01:29.166 --> 01:30.083
Roger that.

10
01:33.083 --> 01:36.291
We're from Special Forces and we're here to rescue you. Follow us.

11
01:41.666 --> 01:43.708
Sir, please help us.

12
01:43.791 --> 01:45.500
We're hostages too, sir.

13
01:45.583 --> 01:47.666
They killed my husband.

14
01:47.750 --> 01:50.250
Commander, we have to take them.

15
01:51.208 --> 01:53.541
Hari, they're not part of our mission.

16
01:55.041 --> 01:57.166
You two, follow me.

17
04:04.125 --> 04:11.125
NEVER SURRENDER

18
04:35.583 --> 04:37.500
Dim! Dimas!

19
04:38.541 --> 04:40.666
You guys want anything?

20
04:41.666 --> 04:42.500
No.

21
04:43.458 --> 04:46.791
He suddenly took us to my grandfather's house and it's in…

22
04:47.583 --> 04:48.708
The middle of nowhere.

23
04:48.791 --> 04:50.916
Beats me where this is, see for yourselves!

24
04:51.541 --> 04:53.708
So what about our getaway plans?

25
04:53.791 --> 04:55.916
It's a no-go?

26
04:58.500 --> 05:01.416
Would you guys mind waiting for me?

27
05:02.375 --> 05:04.833
I shouldn't be too long.

28
05:12.333 --> 05:15.000
Okay then, Put, let us know if you need anything.

29
05:20.541 --> 05:21.916
I don't get you.

30
05:22.666 --> 05:24.958
You wanna go on a getaway with toxic people.

31
05:26.750 --> 05:30.750
Seriously, stop using words you don't even understand.

32
05:30.833 --> 05:32.166
You're such a brat.

33
05:33.333 --> 05:35.250
Hey! You really are a brat.

34
05:35.333 --> 05:37.791
- Do you even know what toxic is? - I do.

35
05:37.875 --> 05:39.250
- Liar. - Fine, come here.

36
05:39.333 --> 05:44.041
Instead of just running your mouth, come take my picture.

37
05:45.583 --> 05:49.583
See? Here we go again. We always end up taking pictures!

38
05:49.666 --> 05:51.125
Just hurry up, will you?

39
05:51.208 --> 05:53.208
Hello, Gus! Gus!

40
05:56.666 --> 05:57.916
Hello, Ben.

41
05:58.000 --> 06:00.416
I'm being serious, Gus. Seriously!

42
06:00.500 --> 06:03.500
So am I. I'm really sorry.

43
06:03.583 --> 06:05.458
It's not funny anymore, Gus.

44
06:06.333 --> 06:09.166
But I also need to put money back into Sari's savings for the kids.

45
06:09.250 --> 06:11.041
Yeah, but not like this, Gus!

46
06:11.125 --> 06:14.625
I want my flash drive back, or I'll call the police!

47
06:15.333 --> 06:16.833
I know you won't.

48
06:17.750 --> 06:20.375
Unless you want to destroy yourself

49
06:21.250 --> 06:23.583
or you want to drag along all those important people too!

50
06:23.666 --> 06:26.208
You bastard! Fuck you, Gus!

51
06:26.833 --> 06:28.708
I'll wait for you at the usual place.

52
07:14.250 --> 07:15.083
Sir.

53
07:15.666 --> 07:16.500
How much?

54
07:17.791 --> 07:19.041
Five hundred.

55
07:20.291 --> 07:21.125
What?

56
07:22.041 --> 07:24.041
Five hundred for ten liters?

57
07:25.250 --> 07:28.333
Gasoline is scarce around here. This is the only place selling it.

58
07:28.416 --> 07:30.208
Check for yourself all around.

59
07:31.000 --> 07:31.833
Hey.

60
07:32.500 --> 07:33.958
This is outrageous price gouging.

61
07:34.041 --> 07:35.583
If you don't like it,

62
07:36.208 --> 07:37.750
call the police…

63
07:38.916 --> 07:40.375
If they're even there.

64
07:49.833 --> 07:50.833
See?

65
08:01.750 --> 08:03.166
Put! Dim!

66
08:04.083 --> 08:05.000
Get in!

67
08:33.208 --> 08:36.291
Dad, are there tigers in places like this?

68
08:37.125 --> 08:38.625
Of course not.

69
08:38.708 --> 08:40.166
There might be snakes.

70
08:40.250 --> 08:42.708
Or if not, then maybe boars.

71
09:03.041 --> 09:03.958
Hey…

72
09:05.041 --> 09:06.250
You guys wait here a minute.

73
09:20.708 --> 09:22.416
This is like the start of a horror movie.

74
09:23.958 --> 09:25.333
Right.

75
09:25.916 --> 09:26.750
Dad…

76
09:31.958 --> 09:33.375
Wow…

77
09:34.666 --> 09:35.500
Hey…

78
09:36.166 --> 09:37.750
- Not too far. - Okay.

79
09:53.166 --> 09:54.166
Wow…

80
10:03.291 --> 10:05.625
No, Dad. This isn't some scheme.

81
10:06.833 --> 10:12.166
Just please look after them for a while. I'm doing this for them anyway.

82
10:14.291 --> 10:16.541
You're not involved in a scam again, are you?

83
10:18.583 --> 10:20.375
I feel sorry for your kids.

84
10:21.750 --> 10:23.958
It's not like that.

85
10:24.041 --> 10:26.041
This is something I really can't walk away from.

86
10:26.125 --> 10:28.416
And you haven't seen them for a while anyway.

87
10:31.166 --> 10:32.750
Just a few days, Dad.

88
10:33.416 --> 10:35.625
As soon as I'm done, I'll pick them up.

89
10:36.875 --> 10:39.916
I wouldn't ask for help if it wasn't really important.

90
10:43.583 --> 10:46.583
Here she is…

91
10:47.166 --> 10:49.916
Come here, Putri, and greet your Grandpa first.

92
11:00.250 --> 11:01.375
Well, Dad?

93
11:03.125 --> 11:05.583
You don't mind, do you?

94
11:18.416 --> 11:19.666
Dim…

95
11:21.375 --> 11:22.250
Dim…

96
11:25.208 --> 11:26.125
Dimas!

97
11:27.375 --> 11:28.375
Dimas!

98
11:30.125 --> 11:30.958
What is it?

99
11:31.833 --> 11:33.041
Give me a hand.

100
11:33.125 --> 11:34.458
Unload the trunk.

101
11:35.958 --> 11:37.458
Okay.

102
11:45.250 --> 11:46.125
Dim…

103
11:47.583 --> 11:49.083
Don't take my bag out.

104
11:50.166 --> 11:51.166
Dim?

105
12:24.333 --> 12:25.250
Mattress.

106
12:26.250 --> 12:27.083
Sheets.

107
12:31.791 --> 12:34.000
Seriously, we're sleeping here?

108
12:37.083 --> 12:38.083
Dad…

109
12:42.458 --> 12:46.250
Dad, there's no cell reception here. You're seriously gonna leave us here?

110
12:46.333 --> 12:48.833
- The room's so ugly. - Dim. Put.

111
12:48.916 --> 12:51.000
You know I have important business to attend to.

112
12:51.083 --> 12:52.583
You guys just chill here.

113
12:52.666 --> 12:55.291
It's not fair, you know I should be on vacation with my friends.

114
12:55.375 --> 12:58.041
Come on, it's been a while since you last saw Grandpa, right?

115
12:58.125 --> 13:00.875
We saw him when Mom died.

116
13:15.583 --> 13:16.708
Three days.

117
13:18.166 --> 13:19.333
Three days max.

118
13:22.250 --> 13:23.208
Come on.

119
13:30.458 --> 13:31.375
Put…

120
14:13.000 --> 14:15.708
You're not here as guests who need to be waited on.

121
14:17.083 --> 14:19.166
All your food comes from this land.

122
14:19.750 --> 14:22.375
So if you don't do your chores, you don't eat.

123
14:24.083 --> 14:25.708
- Chores? - Yes.

124
14:26.416 --> 14:27.541
Get up early,

125
14:28.333 --> 14:29.291
draw some water,

126
14:29.958 --> 14:31.250
milk the cows,

127
14:31.333 --> 14:32.708
work in the garden,

128
14:32.791 --> 14:33.958
pick vegetables,

129
14:34.625 --> 14:36.333
collect eggs from the coop.

130
14:37.500 --> 14:38.500
Lots of things.

131
15:13.416 --> 15:14.416
Do.

132
15:15.625 --> 15:17.166
You take care of Yanus.

133
15:19.375 --> 15:20.583
Will do, Boss.

134
15:23.708 --> 15:25.208
To the children,

135
15:25.291 --> 15:27.875
you can achieve big ambitions.

136
15:27.958 --> 15:31.916
You are the future of this nation.

137
15:53.625 --> 15:54.958
Congratulations, sir.

138
15:55.041 --> 15:56.666
Congratulations to all of us.

139
15:58.041 --> 16:00.250
- Good afternoon, Minister. - Hello.

140
16:00.333 --> 16:01.750
Enjoy your day.

141
16:07.166 --> 16:08.000
Fucker.

142
16:08.083 --> 16:10.250
Well, have you repaired the leak?

143
16:10.833 --> 16:14.125
One is done, the other is still a work in progress.

144
16:15.000 --> 16:16.666
I don't want to end up flooded.

145
16:17.958 --> 16:21.416
It would be a shame to see the business we've built go down the drain.

146
16:24.916 --> 16:26.250
You don't need to worry.

147
16:26.333 --> 16:28.708
The data is secure.

148
16:30.416 --> 16:31.625
That's how it should be.

149
16:37.375 --> 16:38.375
Good afternoon, sir.

150
16:40.750 --> 16:42.208
Fucker!

151
16:43.666 --> 16:44.500
Dimas…

152
17:22.000 --> 17:23.208
Hi, is Grandpa home?

153
17:23.958 --> 17:24.791
What?

154
17:25.625 --> 17:26.708
Is Grandpa home?

155
17:28.083 --> 17:29.333
What?

156
17:31.875 --> 17:32.791
Grandpa.

157
17:33.833 --> 17:36.291
You wanted honey, sir.

158
17:38.791 --> 17:41.041
- What's that, Grandpa? - Honey.

159
17:43.750 --> 17:44.583
Your grandkids?

160
17:48.666 --> 17:50.041
This is Mayang.

161
17:53.875 --> 17:56.458
Her dad is my best friend.

162
17:56.541 --> 18:00.166
I like to get honey and firewood from him.

163
18:00.250 --> 18:02.500
This is Dimas.

164
18:05.500 --> 18:07.166
This is Putri.

165
18:12.708 --> 18:13.625
Dimas.

166
18:14.375 --> 18:15.541
Putri.

167
18:16.416 --> 18:18.166
Wow… So pretty!

168
18:19.458 --> 18:20.291
What, Grandpa?

169
18:22.166 --> 18:23.458
She said your bracelet's pretty.

170
18:23.541 --> 18:25.291
Thanks.

171
18:27.208 --> 18:28.708
Nice to meet you.

172
18:28.791 --> 18:30.916
She said it's nice to meet you guys.

173
18:35.166 --> 18:36.000
I gotta go home.

174
18:36.083 --> 18:37.333
Come on in for a minute.

175
18:45.083 --> 18:45.916
Dimas…

176
18:46.000 --> 18:47.666
- What? - Where are you going?

177
18:47.750 --> 18:49.166
I'm going to take pictures.

178
18:49.250 --> 18:51.041
- Don't go too far. - Okay.

179
18:52.500 --> 18:55.166
- You must be happy. - I am.

180
19:03.500 --> 19:04.875
- Dimas! - Put! Stay there!

181
19:04.958 --> 19:06.583
Dimas, don't move!

182
19:12.000 --> 19:14.000
Stay calm, Dim. Stay calm.

183
19:14.833 --> 19:15.666
Stay calm.

184
19:21.791 --> 19:22.625
Dimas!

185
19:31.708 --> 19:32.541
Dimas!

186
19:37.791 --> 19:38.916
Dimas!

187
19:55.291 --> 19:56.416
Dimas.

188
20:23.083 --> 20:24.583
We have to get out of here.

189
20:29.791 --> 20:31.000
What about Dad?

190
20:31.666 --> 20:34.041
No problem, we'll call him when we get a signal.

191
20:34.791 --> 20:37.416
If he can't pick us up yet, I can ask Tia for help.

192
20:39.375 --> 20:41.250
We can't stay here too long.

193
20:43.291 --> 20:45.166
Grandpa is a bad influence on you.

194
20:50.916 --> 20:53.583
Now I understand why he and Mom weren't close.

195
20:58.208 --> 20:59.833
He's a psycho!

196
21:01.958 --> 21:03.250
You're all packed, right?

197
21:04.791 --> 21:05.916
Let's go.

198
21:06.000 --> 21:07.833
Dimas… Dimas…

199
21:22.125 --> 21:24.083
Dimas! Dimas!

200
21:25.458 --> 21:27.291
- Come on, let's go! - What the…

201
21:27.375 --> 21:28.208
Let's go.

202
21:30.208 --> 21:32.208
Do we really have to leave now?

203
21:32.291 --> 21:34.083
Dimas! Come on!

204
21:34.166 --> 21:37.000
That was the first time I was sleeping well ever since Mom died.

205
21:43.000 --> 21:44.916
Let's just get a signal so I can call Dad.

206
21:45.000 --> 21:45.833
Let's go.

207
21:51.333 --> 21:52.708
My bag!

208
21:52.791 --> 21:54.125
Where's my bag?

209
22:15.375 --> 22:17.583
The number you have dialed cannot be reached.

210
22:17.666 --> 22:19.625
Please try again.

211
22:24.000 --> 22:25.500
Shit, I'm so sorry.

212
22:25.583 --> 22:26.750
Ben…

213
22:26.833 --> 22:28.250
I left the files, so…

214
22:30.541 --> 22:33.375
What did you say, Gus? You left the files?

215
22:41.166 --> 22:43.333
- Are they thugs? - You left the files?

216
22:43.416 --> 22:44.958
You're going to beat me up?

217
22:45.041 --> 22:47.500
I could die here, Gus! Die!

218
22:47.583 --> 22:49.375
I'm not a thug.

219
23:27.708 --> 23:29.208
Hey, I got a signal!

220
23:31.208 --> 23:33.791
The number you have dialed is out of reach.

221
23:33.875 --> 23:35.583
Please try again.

222
23:36.333 --> 23:37.666
- Still not picking up? - No.

223
23:46.083 --> 23:47.000
Morning, miss.

224
23:47.083 --> 23:48.500
Good morning.

225
23:48.583 --> 23:50.000
Can we help you?

226
23:50.791 --> 23:52.875
We want to go back to Jakarta.

227
23:52.958 --> 23:55.791
- Dimas, don't talk to them. - Where's your father?

228
23:55.875 --> 23:58.791
It's okay, sir, thank you. We're just gonna walk.

229
23:58.875 --> 24:00.750
You guys going to the terminal?

230
24:00.833 --> 24:02.250
It's pretty far, miss.

231
24:02.333 --> 24:04.333
About two hours on foot.

232
24:05.166 --> 24:07.125
I can take you on my bike.

233
24:09.208 --> 24:10.166
Two hours?

234
24:16.625 --> 24:18.541
- How much? - That's easy.

235
24:18.625 --> 24:22.708
The thing is, my bike can only carry one person.

236
24:22.791 --> 24:24.583
The suspension is failing.

237
24:24.666 --> 24:26.166
You go first, Putri.

238
24:26.750 --> 24:28.375
If I go first, I might go missing.

239
24:31.208 --> 24:32.083
Well?

240
24:34.500 --> 24:35.750
Okay, fine.

241
24:40.708 --> 24:43.583
Don't go anywhere until he picks you up.

242
24:52.458 --> 24:53.416
Let's go, miss.

243
24:54.000 --> 24:56.666
You can wait here. Have a seat over there.

244
24:59.250 --> 25:00.750
- Ready? - Yes.

245
25:06.541 --> 25:07.500
Miss,

246
25:07.583 --> 25:10.125
I actually have a better bike.

247
25:10.208 --> 25:12.416
Should we go get it?

248
25:13.541 --> 25:15.333
So your brother can ride as well.

249
25:15.416 --> 25:16.875
Yeah, okay.

250
25:18.500 --> 25:20.166
Okay, miss, will do.

251
25:34.166 --> 25:35.708
Putri. Dimas.

252
25:49.625 --> 25:53.000
Your granddaughter is in danger!

253
26:05.083 --> 26:06.541
Your camera looks good.

254
26:06.625 --> 26:08.458
Can I borrow it?

255
26:08.541 --> 26:10.333
- No. - What?

256
26:10.416 --> 26:11.541
- No. - No?

257
26:12.208 --> 26:13.291
- No? - No.

258
26:13.375 --> 26:14.583
Sure, I can!

259
26:18.166 --> 26:19.000
Hey, hey…

260
26:19.083 --> 26:21.333
Where are you going?

261
26:21.416 --> 26:24.666
Hey, you have money in your bag, right?

262
26:24.750 --> 26:25.583
I don't.

263
26:25.666 --> 26:30.041
Help out an orphan. It's very noble to do.

264
26:30.958 --> 26:33.041
Come on, give me your money.

265
26:52.583 --> 26:53.416
Dimas!

266
26:58.333 --> 27:00.708
- Where's your sister? - She went with his friend!

267
27:04.791 --> 27:05.833
Miss, please wait.

268
27:07.458 --> 27:08.833
I'll get the new bike.

269
27:12.958 --> 27:16.416
Relax, your granddaughter is safe with my friend.

270
27:16.500 --> 27:18.166
Where's your friend?

271
27:29.458 --> 27:31.458
Miss, please open the door.

272
27:32.166 --> 27:33.875
I need to push the bike out.

273
27:41.041 --> 27:42.583
Here, take it all.

274
27:44.416 --> 27:48.375
Now tell me, where is your friend, and my granddaughter?

275
27:49.416 --> 27:50.458
Which one is it?

276
27:51.875 --> 27:54.208
- What the-- - Shut up! Shut up.

277
28:04.625 --> 28:06.583
- No, Grandpa, don't-- - Hey!

278
28:07.458 --> 28:09.458
- Dimas! - You can't take it, right?

279
28:14.083 --> 28:15.875
Wake up! Hey, wake up.

280
28:47.500 --> 28:48.916
You motherfucker!

281
29:00.000 --> 29:02.250
I'll ask you again. Where is my granddaughter?

282
29:02.333 --> 29:06.541
Okay, sir! Have mercy, please!

283
29:06.625 --> 29:08.666
Dimas, are you okay?

284
29:13.833 --> 29:16.125
- Let go! Let me go! - Where are you going? Stay still!

285
29:24.291 --> 29:29.000
You motherfucker!

286
29:30.291 --> 29:31.125
Putri!

287
29:31.208 --> 29:34.083
Putri, that's enough!

288
29:36.291 --> 29:38.166
- Motherfucker! - Putri, it's okay.

289
29:38.250 --> 29:39.833
Are you all right?

290
29:41.000 --> 29:42.458
Let's go home. Go.

291
29:42.541 --> 29:43.833
Come on, go.

292
29:45.208 --> 29:47.125
- Bastard! - Grandpa!

293
30:13.833 --> 30:16.916
I'm sorry that happened to you this morning.

294
30:25.041 --> 30:26.250
But I'm proud of you.

295
30:28.875 --> 30:31.208
You are brave, just like your mother.

296
30:49.208 --> 30:51.625
But please, open!

297
30:51.708 --> 30:54.916
Okay, so today Putri and…

298
30:55.000 --> 30:56.583
Putri's mom.

299
30:56.666 --> 30:58.833
We're making a dish…

300
30:59.500 --> 31:01.500
- Should I say it? - Yes.

301
31:01.583 --> 31:03.791
Barbell cake. No, wait.

302
31:03.875 --> 31:05.791
- Marble! - Marble!

303
31:05.875 --> 31:07.250
Marble cake!

304
31:07.333 --> 31:09.541
See, I can't really do the talk.

305
31:09.625 --> 31:11.791
That's okay, we need to make memories.

306
31:11.875 --> 31:14.541
Okay, so I wanna go over the ingredients.

307
31:14.625 --> 31:16.791
Mom, take them over there. Show them.

308
31:16.875 --> 31:18.583
- I should hold these up? - Yes, show them.

309
32:29.958 --> 32:32.375
The minister asked after you, little brother.

310
32:47.208 --> 32:48.375
Right…

311
32:48.458 --> 32:49.875
By the way,

312
32:51.083 --> 32:53.208
I know about the accountant.

313
32:58.958 --> 33:01.875
Another victim without a second thought.

314
33:03.541 --> 33:06.416
You can't keep killing people like that.

315
33:16.208 --> 33:17.041
Hey.

316
33:17.708 --> 33:18.958
Look me in the eye.

317
33:29.750 --> 33:31.750
You're too impulsive.

318
33:32.750 --> 33:34.333
About Yanus,

319
33:34.416 --> 33:36.958
we all know he had to be eliminated.

320
33:37.041 --> 33:38.458
But the accountant?

321
33:39.333 --> 33:41.583
There was no reason to get rid of him.

322
33:42.583 --> 33:43.875
Remember, little brother.

323
33:44.541 --> 33:45.625
Everything

324
33:46.666 --> 33:48.291
requires a strategy.

325
33:51.416 --> 33:52.250
Okay.

326
33:53.416 --> 33:54.500
Next time,

327
33:55.500 --> 33:57.375
I won't be impulsive.

328
34:15.875 --> 34:18.125
So you know where the data is?

329
34:20.541 --> 34:21.625
Around Dieng.

330
34:22.708 --> 34:24.166
I'll go there tonight.

331
34:24.250 --> 34:25.833
Take Derry and Iyang.

332
34:27.000 --> 34:29.416
I don't need babysitters.

333
34:32.250 --> 34:33.625
Bastian Yamakala!

334
34:38.625 --> 34:39.625
Did you forget?

335
35:00.916 --> 35:01.791
Take care.

336
36:32.666 --> 36:35.333
Pick the red ones. Leave the others.

337
36:36.125 --> 36:38.750
- What if it's red but small? Is that okay? - That's fine.

338
36:40.833 --> 36:42.458
When was the last time you practiced?

339
36:42.541 --> 36:45.125
It's been a while. Since Mom got sick.

340
36:45.208 --> 36:46.916
- Dimas! - Hey.

341
36:55.666 --> 36:57.875
Droppings! Grandpa!

342
36:57.958 --> 36:59.416
- What's wrong? - Grandpa, help!

343
36:59.500 --> 37:00.750
Just leave it.

344
37:12.916 --> 37:14.041
Again.

345
37:19.666 --> 37:22.041
Dimas, this looks like it needs one-- Watch out!

346
37:24.416 --> 37:25.666
Careful.

347
37:26.625 --> 37:28.166
You didn't place it quite right.

348
37:32.583 --> 37:34.208
Take a strong stance.

349
37:34.791 --> 37:36.833
This should be straight, okay?

350
37:38.208 --> 37:39.291
Control your breathing.

351
37:39.375 --> 37:41.750
Put your hands like this.

352
37:41.833 --> 37:43.625
From top to bottom.

353
37:43.708 --> 37:46.750
- Top to bottom. Got it? - Yeah, got it.

354
37:46.833 --> 37:48.833
Put, wanna try?

355
37:48.916 --> 37:51.583
- No, let Dimas do it. - Have a go, it's easy.

356
37:51.666 --> 37:53.666
- No need. Just Dimas. - Even Dimas can do it.

357
37:55.000 --> 37:55.833
Release.

358
38:11.875 --> 38:13.375
Wow.

359
38:13.458 --> 38:16.208
This might be the best milk I've ever had.

360
38:16.291 --> 38:17.708
Agreed.

361
38:17.791 --> 38:19.458
Carton milk doesn't even come close.

362
38:20.750 --> 38:22.875
Here, eat.

363
38:22.958 --> 38:25.333
If you need more rice, there's more in the back.

364
38:27.125 --> 38:28.666
The egg dish that Mom used to make!

365
38:28.750 --> 38:29.583
Yeah.

366
38:33.000 --> 38:35.166
Hey… Finish everything.

367
38:35.250 --> 38:37.833
After this, I have more jobs for you to do.

368
38:59.708 --> 39:01.125
Hey…

369
39:01.208 --> 39:02.166
Put.

370
39:02.250 --> 39:03.083
Yes, Grandpa?

371
39:06.666 --> 39:07.666
What is it?

372
39:13.500 --> 39:15.625
I have something for you.

373
39:19.458 --> 39:23.041
I was always absent during your mother's important moments.

374
39:24.458 --> 39:26.666
But when my first grandchild was born,

375
39:28.708 --> 39:30.250
I had to be there.

376
39:33.416 --> 39:36.416
You can keep it for when you miss her.

377
39:43.333 --> 39:44.541
All right, then.

378
39:44.625 --> 39:46.291
I have things to do.

379
39:47.833 --> 39:49.166
By the way,

380
39:49.833 --> 39:53.083
if you need anything,

381
39:53.708 --> 39:56.791
just come get me.

382
39:59.875 --> 40:00.875
Grandpa, wait.

383
40:04.458 --> 40:05.375
Hold on.

384
40:08.916 --> 40:12.000
Now we can both keep it.

385
40:17.541 --> 40:19.291
You're so young here.

386
40:19.375 --> 40:21.500
- You still had black hair. - Right.

387
40:45.250 --> 40:46.291
Hi.

388
40:49.916 --> 40:52.166
Are you looking for Grandpa?

389
40:53.125 --> 40:57.458
He's back there with my brother, fishing.

390
40:57.541 --> 40:59.416
Right there.

391
40:59.500 --> 41:02.333
It's okay. I can leave the corn on the porch.

392
41:04.250 --> 41:05.250
It's okay.

393
41:07.541 --> 41:08.875
My God…

394
41:09.458 --> 41:11.500
Come on, that's nothing.

395
41:12.791 --> 41:14.625
My nuts almost popped.

396
41:43.833 --> 41:44.791
Putri.

397
41:45.375 --> 41:46.666
Signal?

398
41:49.083 --> 41:50.375
Signal?

399
41:50.458 --> 41:53.333
Cell reception?

400
41:53.916 --> 41:55.666
I know. Over there.

401
41:55.750 --> 41:58.208
There's reception there?

402
41:58.291 --> 41:59.291
Let's go!

403
42:00.958 --> 42:03.041
- Over there? - Right there.

404
42:15.500 --> 42:16.833
Good afternoon, gentlemen.

405
42:18.541 --> 42:20.375
I'm looking for a relative of mine.

406
42:20.458 --> 42:22.583
He's staying at his in-law's house.

407
42:22.666 --> 42:26.750
He has his children with him, a boy and a girl.

408
42:26.833 --> 42:28.250
Maybe you've seen them?

409
42:31.333 --> 42:32.583
Do you have a picture of them?

410
42:33.166 --> 42:34.083
A picture?

411
42:35.916 --> 42:36.833
I do.

412
42:48.208 --> 42:49.625
We know them.

413
43:04.833 --> 43:08.208
- We miss you! - Well, Put, did you get home?

414
43:08.291 --> 43:11.875
No. I think I'll be here for a while.

415
43:13.000 --> 43:15.250
Yeah, I can't reach my dad.

416
43:15.333 --> 43:16.958
I see.

417
43:17.041 --> 43:18.875
Okay, then.

418
43:19.875 --> 43:21.583
Hey, where are you guys?

419
43:22.250 --> 43:24.416
We're at… We are…

420
43:24.500 --> 43:26.916
Let's switch to video.

421
43:27.875 --> 43:29.083
We'll do a video call.

422
43:33.625 --> 43:36.000
- You don't have to. I understand. - Put…

423
43:36.666 --> 43:37.750
"For Life," my ass.

424
43:50.875 --> 43:52.666
Putri, are you okay?

425
43:52.750 --> 43:53.750
I'm fine.

426
44:07.500 --> 44:09.000
So do you know where they are?

427
44:10.000 --> 44:11.875
I do, I do.

428
44:15.375 --> 44:17.916
Grandpa, it's been an hour.

429
44:18.000 --> 44:20.250
Why don't we use a net and make it easier?

430
44:20.333 --> 44:22.208
It's not that simple.

431
44:22.291 --> 44:24.833
If we cast the net and fail,

432
44:24.916 --> 44:27.416
the fish escape and we don't eat.

433
44:29.208 --> 44:31.833
This will teach you to be patient.

434
44:32.583 --> 44:36.291
With patience, we can plan things properly,

435
44:37.083 --> 44:39.500
and we can defeat any powerful enemy.

436
44:44.708 --> 44:45.875
Come on, let's go.

437
44:45.958 --> 44:49.041
How about we handle the next job?

438
44:51.375 --> 44:54.000
That way, the boss will have a reason to give us a raise, right?

439
44:54.083 --> 44:55.291
I agree.

440
44:56.083 --> 44:59.166
My back hurts from digging so many graves.

441
45:13.458 --> 45:14.291
What is it?

442
45:14.375 --> 45:17.541
You want to throw away the bracelet? No! What a waste.

443
45:18.208 --> 45:19.458
What?

444
45:26.125 --> 45:29.250
Don't throw it away. It's a waste.

445
45:36.875 --> 45:39.833
I don't want to wear it anymore.

446
45:40.750 --> 45:41.625
Still a waste.

447
45:45.708 --> 45:48.291
You can have it. Want it?

448
45:48.375 --> 45:50.000
For me?

449
45:53.208 --> 45:54.041
Thank you.

450
46:02.458 --> 46:03.458
Putri.

451
46:04.333 --> 46:05.666
Who is that? She's pretty.

452
46:06.666 --> 46:07.708
Who is that?

453
46:09.791 --> 46:10.916
This one…

454
46:13.916 --> 46:18.875
This is my… My mother.

455
46:18.958 --> 46:20.916
My mother.

456
46:21.000 --> 46:23.541
But she's not around anymore. She's…

457
46:26.375 --> 46:27.541
She died.

458
46:44.291 --> 46:47.416
My parents are gone too. Your grandpa was my dad's commander.

459
46:47.500 --> 46:49.666
My dad asked him to move here.

460
46:49.750 --> 46:53.000
Then I got close to Mr. Hari. Now your grandpa takes care of me.

461
46:59.083 --> 47:01.458
Putri, lunch is ready.

462
47:01.541 --> 47:03.000
Yes, I'll be right there.

463
47:03.875 --> 47:06.708
Mayang, wanna eat together?

464
47:07.291 --> 47:08.500
Eat together.

465
47:08.583 --> 47:09.583
Let's go.

466
47:28.791 --> 47:31.916
Thank God they ended up fine yesterday.

467
47:34.000 --> 47:35.541
You know what?

468
47:35.625 --> 47:39.791
It was Mayang who told me you guys were in danger yesterday.

469
47:40.458 --> 47:42.416
Good thing Mayang saw you guys.

470
47:43.791 --> 47:46.666
Grandpa, how do you sign thank you?

471
47:47.916 --> 47:48.833
Thank you.

472
47:48.916 --> 47:50.958
- Thank you. - Thank you.

473
47:51.041 --> 47:52.500
You're welcome.

474
47:53.541 --> 47:54.541
You're welcome.

475
48:01.833 --> 48:04.083
Mayang says that while you're here,

476
48:04.166 --> 48:05.916
be wary of other people.

477
48:09.375 --> 48:11.458
Just keep going straight ahead.

478
48:11.541 --> 48:13.958
You'll eventually get to the old man's house.

479
48:14.041 --> 48:15.583
Thank you.

480
48:15.666 --> 48:18.041
Because not everyone here is good.

481
48:19.875 --> 48:21.125
Be careful.

482
48:21.208 --> 48:22.416
Be careful.

483
48:23.791 --> 48:25.041
Be careful.

484
48:28.041 --> 48:30.708
So I can go home now, right?

485
48:30.791 --> 48:33.375
Hold on… hold on.

486
48:37.166 --> 48:38.333
Thank you.

487
48:39.375 --> 48:40.583
You're welcome!

488
48:53.250 --> 48:55.750
Mayang, take care.

489
50:22.583 --> 50:24.500
No, please don't.

490
50:41.541 --> 50:44.291
No, please no.

491
52:05.166 --> 52:06.416
Good afternoon, sir.

492
52:07.083 --> 52:08.583
My car broke down.

493
52:09.458 --> 52:10.916
Can you please help me?

494
52:12.666 --> 52:14.500
I'll get some equipment.

495
52:17.458 --> 52:19.625
May I come in?

496
52:22.333 --> 52:24.833
- Please, come in. - Thanks. Sorry to bother you.

497
52:44.083 --> 52:45.083
May I sit down?

498
52:46.416 --> 52:48.166
I had to walk quite far.

499
52:50.000 --> 52:50.833
Go ahead.

500
52:51.500 --> 52:52.416
Thank you.

501
54:16.583 --> 54:17.666
Where's the car?

502
54:21.500 --> 54:23.000
Near the T-intersection.

503
54:26.833 --> 54:28.250
Let's go.

504
54:50.791 --> 54:54.041
Be careful.

505
55:14.583 --> 55:15.833
Keys.

506
55:21.750 --> 55:22.583
What's going on?

507
55:23.416 --> 55:24.916
We have to go after Grandpa.

508
55:25.000 --> 55:26.791
Help me! Help me find the keys!

509
55:26.875 --> 55:28.083
The keys to the motorcycle!

510
55:53.750 --> 55:55.666
I got this from an insider.

511
55:57.125 --> 56:00.500
Agus's father-in-law is no ordinary man.

512
56:08.541 --> 56:10.583
Full name, Haris Prastowo.

513
56:11.250 --> 56:14.166
Born in Salatiga, 1966.

514
56:14.875 --> 56:16.708
Ex-Special Forces.

515
56:17.791 --> 56:19.833
His last rank was pretty high.

516
56:33.625 --> 56:35.458
In 2004,

517
56:36.583 --> 56:38.083
he was suddenly dismissed?

518
56:42.375 --> 56:44.833
Hold on, this won't take long.

519
56:57.458 --> 56:58.583
Dismissed?

520
57:06.000 --> 57:07.541
What did you do to that girl?

521
57:12.500 --> 57:14.041
What do you mean, sir?

522
57:17.333 --> 57:18.333
I mean,

523
57:19.208 --> 57:20.708
if she's alive,

524
57:20.791 --> 57:22.083
I'll let you live.

525
57:22.916 --> 57:24.041
But if she's not,

526
57:24.708 --> 57:28.458
you'll regret you ever knew me for the rest of your life.

527
57:29.750 --> 57:31.083
You have a sharp eye, sir.

528
58:11.250 --> 58:12.666
Just take it easy, Bas.

529
58:13.875 --> 58:15.125
I'll handle this.

530
58:17.541 --> 58:19.125
Just relax-- Fuck!

531
58:20.375 --> 58:21.583
Shit!

532
58:43.666 --> 58:44.583
Calm down.

533
58:45.541 --> 58:47.041
We can talk about this calmly.

534
58:47.750 --> 58:48.875
I'll ask you one more time.

535
58:50.625 --> 58:52.333
What did you do with the girl?

536
01:02:42.083 --> 01:02:43.250
Putri, there are dead bodies.

537
01:03:24.958 --> 01:03:26.500
Bastard… fuck!

538
01:03:59.416 --> 01:04:01.583
You really are a match for me, motherfucker!

539
01:05:38.583 --> 01:05:40.000
Fuck you!

540
01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:32.375
Fuck you!

541
01:08:32.416 --> 01:08:33.708
- Grandpa! - Grandpa!

542
01:08:36.333 --> 01:08:37.250
- Grandpa! - Grandpa!

543
01:10:02.250 --> 01:10:03.500
What do you want?

544
01:10:10.208 --> 01:10:11.916
What do you want?

545
01:10:19.500 --> 01:10:21.375
Okay, okay, okay.

546
01:10:26.250 --> 01:10:29.583
I want to retrieve the data your son-in-law stole.

547
01:10:32.625 --> 01:10:34.625
- What data? - What data?

548
01:10:36.583 --> 01:10:38.458
What data?

549
01:10:42.833 --> 01:10:44.000
Okay…

550
01:10:44.625 --> 01:10:45.833
Money…

551
01:10:45.916 --> 01:10:47.416
Cash flow.

552
01:10:48.541 --> 01:10:50.000
Extortion money,

553
01:10:50.625 --> 01:10:51.791
protection money,

554
01:10:52.833 --> 01:10:54.000
bribes

555
01:10:55.250 --> 01:10:58.541
for those who're looking to get a seat in Parliament.

556
01:11:01.375 --> 01:11:03.333
If that data leaks,

557
01:11:04.625 --> 01:11:06.625
many prominent figures

558
01:11:07.416 --> 01:11:10.125
would have their dirty secrets exposed.

559
01:11:13.583 --> 01:11:15.000
Why would Agus want that?

560
01:11:15.666 --> 01:11:17.333
- Why would Agus take it… - Why?

561
01:11:21.875 --> 01:11:23.750
For money, dammit!

562
01:11:23.833 --> 01:11:24.875
To blackmail Ben.

563
01:11:25.750 --> 01:11:27.166
Why else would he take it?

564
01:11:29.458 --> 01:11:31.291
Your son-in-law needs money

565
01:11:32.500 --> 01:11:33.750
to replace

566
01:11:34.875 --> 01:11:37.458
the money that his wife had left behind, which was lost

567
01:11:38.500 --> 01:11:39.458
to online gambling.

568
01:11:49.750 --> 01:11:50.916
It won't be long now.

569
01:11:52.625 --> 01:11:54.333
This place will be surrounded.

570
01:11:55.750 --> 01:11:58.791
You, your sweet grandchildren…

571
01:12:00.208 --> 01:12:01.375
will be dead.

572
01:12:37.291 --> 01:12:39.000
Grandpa, what do we do now?

573
01:12:39.083 --> 01:12:41.291
- Should we look for Dad? - How is Dad?

574
01:12:41.375 --> 01:12:43.208
Let's just call the police, Grandpa.

575
01:12:45.500 --> 01:12:46.833
We can't do that, Put.

576
01:12:48.875 --> 01:12:50.458
We have to think this through.

577
01:12:51.416 --> 01:12:55.000
If the police are involved, things will end up more complicated.

578
01:12:57.250 --> 01:12:58.583
If he's telling the truth,

579
01:12:59.666 --> 01:13:01.541
your father has broken the law.

580
01:13:08.583 --> 01:13:10.541
Not to mention there are many casualties now.

581
01:13:11.416 --> 01:13:13.291
I'll definitely be a suspect too.

582
01:13:23.250 --> 01:13:24.125
Put…

583
01:13:28.750 --> 01:13:30.666
I'll find a way out from all of this.

584
01:13:30.750 --> 01:13:32.416
I'll make sure you guys are safe.

585
01:13:35.166 --> 01:13:37.541
For now, we need to focus on what we have to do.

586
01:13:38.250 --> 01:13:39.125
Mayang.

587
01:13:40.166 --> 01:13:42.500
We must give her a proper burial.

588
01:13:43.583 --> 01:13:45.625
The poor girl doesn't have anyone else.

589
01:13:52.833 --> 01:13:54.083
Dimas!

590
01:14:06.125 --> 01:14:08.333
Putri! Dimas! Run!

591
01:14:14.833 --> 01:14:16.958
Dimas! What are you doing?

592
01:14:17.041 --> 01:14:18.541
- What the fuck? - What are you doing?

593
01:14:18.625 --> 01:14:21.458
- Grandpa's in danger! - Don't act like a tough guy!

594
01:14:21.541 --> 01:14:22.791
Stay still!

595
01:15:04.166 --> 01:15:05.166
- Grandpa! - Grandpa!

596
01:15:23.375 --> 01:15:24.208
Get back!

597
01:15:24.291 --> 01:15:25.125
Grandpa!

598
01:15:25.208 --> 01:15:26.041
Dimas!

599
01:16:15.500 --> 01:16:16.500
Bas… Pick up, Bas.

600
01:17:28.291 --> 01:17:29.208
Hello.

601
01:17:29.791 --> 01:17:30.625
Bas.

602
01:17:49.416 --> 01:17:52.375
Mr. Haris Prastowo?

603
01:17:53.083 --> 01:17:54.458
Where's the owner of this phone?

604
01:17:54.958 --> 01:17:56.875
The owner of this phone came here,

605
01:17:56.958 --> 01:17:59.583
killed innocent people, and threatened my family.

606
01:18:01.291 --> 01:18:04.416
But he's paid for everything with his own life.

607
01:18:13.875 --> 01:18:15.500
You wanna mess with me?

608
01:18:20.833 --> 01:18:22.333
You know this guy?

609
01:18:22.416 --> 01:18:24.083
You must know him.

610
01:18:26.583 --> 01:18:27.750
Talk!

611
01:18:28.916 --> 01:18:29.833
Dad…

612
01:18:31.208 --> 01:18:32.041
Dad…

613
01:18:33.916 --> 01:18:35.458
Dad…

614
01:18:37.083 --> 01:18:38.625
Where are Putri and Dimas?

615
01:18:43.208 --> 01:18:45.250
- Dad… Dad! - Dad!

616
01:18:45.333 --> 01:18:46.500
Dad!

617
01:18:46.583 --> 01:18:47.583
Putri…

618
01:18:48.208 --> 01:18:49.208
Dimas…

619
01:18:50.666 --> 01:18:52.041
I'm sorry.

620
01:18:53.208 --> 01:18:54.125
I…

621
01:18:54.708 --> 01:18:56.500
haven't been

622
01:18:56.583 --> 01:18:58.000
a good father.

623
01:19:21.708 --> 01:19:22.958
I'm sorry.

624
01:19:24.083 --> 01:19:26.916
I love you guys.

625
01:19:32.208 --> 01:19:33.666
Dad!

626
01:20:24.208 --> 01:20:26.000
Take this money. Go far away.

627
01:20:28.125 --> 01:20:31.166
If I don't contact you guys in 48 hours,

628
01:20:32.083 --> 01:20:33.166
here.

629
01:20:34.250 --> 01:20:35.583
Call this number.

630
01:20:36.916 --> 01:20:39.208
Mention my name and ask for help.

631
01:20:40.958 --> 01:20:44.000
But if I can take care all of this,

632
01:20:45.083 --> 01:20:46.666
I will contact you.

633
01:20:50.583 --> 01:20:52.708
Why don't we all just go together, Grandpa?

634
01:20:54.791 --> 01:20:56.208
This place isn't safe now.

635
01:20:56.291 --> 01:20:58.375
We can't tell anyone nor report it to the police.

636
01:20:58.458 --> 01:21:00.208
Let's just all go together.

637
01:21:00.791 --> 01:21:02.500
They killed Dad already!

638
01:21:04.833 --> 01:21:06.291
I will deal with them all.

639
01:21:06.375 --> 01:21:08.541
Why do you have to deal with it?

640
01:21:08.625 --> 01:21:10.833
You just want to kill people, right?

641
01:21:14.458 --> 01:21:15.583
It's not that, Put.

642
01:21:17.291 --> 01:21:19.500
I'm staying right here for you guys too.

643
01:21:20.333 --> 01:21:21.666
If we run away…

644
01:21:23.416 --> 01:21:25.041
we'll keep running.

645
01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:28.166
And we'll never solve the problem.

646
01:21:37.000 --> 01:21:38.833
If you die, what happens to us?

647
01:21:52.250 --> 01:21:54.791
Everything must be taken care of here.

648
01:22:54.625 --> 01:22:56.000
Where are we going, Putri?

649
01:22:56.791 --> 01:22:57.666
I don't know.

650
01:22:58.291 --> 01:23:00.208
Maybe find the closest police station.

651
01:23:00.708 --> 01:23:03.291
When the police arrive, Grandpa may already be dead.

652
01:23:08.375 --> 01:23:10.458
Then what do you want to do, Dimas?

653
01:23:10.541 --> 01:23:12.375
- You wanna stay and fight them? - Yes!

654
01:23:14.458 --> 01:23:17.875
Can you at least try to understand what things are like right now?

655
01:23:18.666 --> 01:23:19.500
Dad's gone.

656
01:23:19.583 --> 01:23:21.125
- Our life-- - Has never been the same

657
01:23:21.208 --> 01:23:22.291
since Mom died!

658
01:23:25.166 --> 01:23:26.791
Now we only have Grandpa.

659
01:23:26.875 --> 01:23:28.625
Do we really want to leave him too?

660
01:23:32.666 --> 01:23:35.000
- What if we die? - If we die, we die!

661
01:23:36.250 --> 01:23:39.333
All that matters is that we're a family, we stay with Grandpa!

662
01:24:11.500 --> 01:24:12.750
We've made a decision.

663
01:24:14.958 --> 01:24:16.333
We're not leaving.

664
01:24:18.958 --> 01:24:20.500
We want to be here with you.

665
01:24:23.166 --> 01:24:24.625
Now you just need to tell

666
01:24:25.708 --> 01:24:27.916
me and Dimas what we need to do.

667
01:24:41.750 --> 01:24:43.541
We hit them back.

668
01:25:02.750 --> 01:25:04.250
Commander!

669
01:25:04.333 --> 01:25:07.625
What a pleasant surprise. How are you?

670
01:25:07.708 --> 01:25:10.083
Ton, I don't have much time.

671
01:25:10.833 --> 01:25:12.291
I need information.

672
01:25:13.458 --> 01:25:14.750
You know who Ulo is?

673
01:25:16.208 --> 01:25:19.916
Ulo? Permission to speak, Commander.

674
01:25:20.000 --> 01:25:21.833
What business do you have with him?

675
01:25:24.708 --> 01:25:26.250
What do you know about him?

676
01:25:30.041 --> 01:25:32.333
Ulo's real name is Agustinus Yamakala.

677
01:25:32.958 --> 01:25:35.083
He's the eldest son of Bobby Yamakala,

678
01:25:35.166 --> 01:25:37.333
who led a community organization during the New Order.

679
01:25:38.708 --> 01:25:41.708
He poses as a lawyer, but he's actually a land scammer.

680
01:25:43.166 --> 01:25:45.083
After Bobby died,

681
01:25:45.166 --> 01:25:47.458
Ulo took over his father's business

682
01:25:47.541 --> 01:25:50.208
together with his younger brother, Bastianus.

683
01:25:54.041 --> 01:25:55.125
Education?

684
01:25:55.208 --> 01:25:56.875
As far as I know, Commander,

685
01:25:56.958 --> 01:25:59.500
he attended military academy but didn't graduate.

686
01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:03.583
And his younger brother, Bastianus, who went to school overseas,

687
01:26:03.666 --> 01:26:06.166
often clashed with their father because…

688
01:26:07.291 --> 01:26:08.958
Well, emotional disorders.

689
01:26:15.375 --> 01:26:17.083
And because of this,

690
01:26:17.166 --> 01:26:19.333
Bastianus is usually kept out of sight.

691
01:26:19.416 --> 01:26:22.875
Ulo handles their day-to-day operations.

692
01:26:30.750 --> 01:26:31.583
Put…

693
01:26:43.708 --> 01:26:47.583
He started out as a land scammer and eventually became a hired thug.

694
01:26:49.041 --> 01:26:52.500
So if there's a need for violence, Ulo's the go-to guy.

695
01:26:53.833 --> 01:26:55.916
His areas of operation include extortion,

696
01:26:56.000 --> 01:26:59.541
intimidation, bribery, and the forcible seizure of land.

697
01:27:00.333 --> 01:27:02.416
He does everything with his team.

698
01:27:14.625 --> 01:27:15.916
How big is his team?

699
01:27:16.708 --> 01:27:18.708
I don't know for sure, Commander.

700
01:27:18.791 --> 01:27:20.458
But one thing's for sure.

701
01:27:20.541 --> 01:27:21.666
Lately,

702
01:27:22.375 --> 01:27:23.416
for the right price,

703
01:27:24.083 --> 01:27:27.125
he and his team can be hired for campaign security and…

704
01:27:28.250 --> 01:27:29.833
instigation.

705
01:28:01.166 --> 01:28:02.000
Sir…

706
01:28:02.083 --> 01:28:04.916
Please take this to a safe place.

707
01:28:05.000 --> 01:28:07.000
- Yes, sir. - Thank you.

708
01:28:08.125 --> 01:28:10.708
Permission to speak, sir. I apologize for being presumptuous.

709
01:28:10.791 --> 01:28:12.583
What business do you have with them?

710
01:28:14.000 --> 01:28:15.750
They're very dangerous people.

711
01:28:16.625 --> 01:28:18.750
I'll explain when all this is over.

712
01:28:19.875 --> 01:28:20.791
Thank you, Ton.

713
01:28:30.708 --> 01:28:31.791
Slow down.

714
01:28:32.875 --> 01:28:36.208
Are we eating here so we can maintain the perimeter?

715
01:28:37.208 --> 01:28:38.125
No.

716
01:28:39.375 --> 01:28:41.500
So you can see that.

717
01:28:43.583 --> 01:28:45.375
You can't see that in Jakarta.

718
01:28:47.083 --> 01:28:48.083
Too much smog.

719
01:28:48.166 --> 01:28:49.333
So right.

720
01:28:51.666 --> 01:28:53.916
Eat. You guys need energy.

721
01:29:01.958 --> 01:29:02.958
Grandpa.

722
01:29:03.041 --> 01:29:05.000
What's with the scar on your face?

723
01:29:06.000 --> 01:29:07.916
- Did you get that during a war? - Dimas!

724
01:29:23.375 --> 01:29:25.583
Grandpa, Mom used to tell us.

725
01:29:28.791 --> 01:29:32.166
She said whenever you went away, you'd be gone for months at a time.

726
01:29:34.166 --> 01:29:38.916
And when you came back, you'd shut yourself in your room for ages.

727
01:29:42.250 --> 01:29:43.416
Did you need healing?

728
01:29:49.500 --> 01:29:51.291
I used to think so.

729
01:29:53.208 --> 01:29:56.375
But it turns out there are things that can't be healed.

730
01:29:56.458 --> 01:29:59.083
- Sir! Sir… - Let me go with you, sir.

731
01:30:02.291 --> 01:30:05.291
One time, while on a mission…

732
01:30:08.166 --> 01:30:10.166
I was faced with two options.

733
01:30:12.208 --> 01:30:16.208
Doing what I thought was right…

734
01:30:16.291 --> 01:30:17.458
Get in!

735
01:30:18.375 --> 01:30:19.708
Hurry, let's go!

736
01:30:20.291 --> 01:30:21.208
Get in!

737
01:30:21.291 --> 01:30:22.291
Hurry!

738
01:30:23.541 --> 01:30:24.500
Let's go.

739
01:30:25.458 --> 01:30:26.541
Commander.

740
01:30:30.041 --> 01:30:33.750
Hari, I already told you they're not part of our mission.

741
01:30:33.833 --> 01:30:36.166
You almost put us all in danger!

742
01:30:37.041 --> 01:30:38.208
Leave them!

743
01:30:39.958 --> 01:30:41.541
…or follow orders.

744
01:30:43.333 --> 01:30:45.791
Sir, don't leave us!

745
01:30:46.750 --> 01:30:48.291
- Sir! - Let's move!

746
01:30:48.875 --> 01:30:49.875
Sir!

747
01:30:49.958 --> 01:30:52.083
- Sir… - Come on, son.

748
01:30:52.166 --> 01:30:53.375
I'm sorry.

749
01:30:55.625 --> 01:30:58.416
Sir! Don't leave us, sir!

750
01:30:58.500 --> 01:31:00.750
- Sir! - Come now…

751
01:31:07.666 --> 01:31:09.416
Run, son! Run!

752
01:31:17.541 --> 01:31:18.375
No!

753
01:31:24.291 --> 01:31:26.083
No!

754
01:31:34.791 --> 01:31:35.875
Grandpa, I'm sorry.

755
01:31:36.875 --> 01:31:37.958
Yesterday,

756
01:31:38.041 --> 01:31:40.916
I said you only wanted to kill people.

757
01:31:45.625 --> 01:31:47.791
But Grandpa's really gonna kill more people.

758
01:31:48.583 --> 01:31:49.416
Dimas!

759
01:31:55.666 --> 01:31:57.958
I lived without purpose for a long time.

760
01:31:59.250 --> 01:32:00.666
I just followed orders.

761
01:32:02.541 --> 01:32:05.791
That affected the relationship between me and your mother.

762
01:32:07.875 --> 01:32:09.333
But now I know

763
01:32:10.375 --> 01:32:12.791
why I'm still alive.

764
01:32:14.000 --> 01:32:16.333
I want to do the right thing.

765
01:32:18.250 --> 01:32:20.041
Protect the two of you.

766
01:32:38.833 --> 01:32:40.958
Grandpa is just like Mom, right, Dimas?

767
01:32:43.750 --> 01:32:44.958
Braised soy sauce eggs,

768
01:32:46.125 --> 01:32:48.125
loves to look at the stars,

769
01:32:50.125 --> 01:32:52.791
and also, this is the weirdest,

770
01:32:53.583 --> 01:32:55.500
likes to listen to keroncong music.

771
01:32:58.250 --> 01:33:00.458
That's why you can take it easy now.

772
01:33:00.541 --> 01:33:02.541
We'll take care of you. Right, Putri?

773
01:33:24.416 --> 01:33:26.958
What happens if we kill people tomorrow, Dimas?

774
01:33:32.833 --> 01:33:34.375
It will be self-defense.

775
01:33:37.583 --> 01:33:39.083
Don't overthink it.

776
01:33:40.458 --> 01:33:41.875
Just pray for forgiveness.

777
01:34:30.166 --> 01:34:31.500
This is Dad's.

778
01:34:59.541 --> 01:35:02.125
If it wasn't for me, maybe Dad would still be alive.

779
01:35:02.750 --> 01:35:05.083
I'm such an idiot. Why did I take his bag out? Why?

780
01:35:05.166 --> 01:35:06.750
- Dimas… - Hey…

781
01:35:06.833 --> 01:35:08.416
- Dimas… - Moron!

782
01:35:08.500 --> 01:35:10.625
Hey, stop! Stop.

783
01:35:10.708 --> 01:35:13.041
Stop it. Stop blaming yourself, okay?

784
01:35:13.791 --> 01:35:16.708
It's already happened. There's no way you could have known.

785
01:35:16.791 --> 01:35:19.875
Grandpa, what if we just give them the files?

786
01:35:20.875 --> 01:35:22.041
Doesn't work that way.

787
01:35:22.958 --> 01:35:24.833
They won't stop until we're dead.

788
01:36:09.291 --> 01:36:10.625
Dear God.

789
01:36:14.250 --> 01:36:17.000
I surrender myself to You.

790
01:36:19.416 --> 01:36:22.916
Because only You have the power of life, Father.

791
01:36:27.875 --> 01:36:29.166
Please guide

792
01:36:30.250 --> 01:36:32.375
and lead Your servant

793
01:36:33.541 --> 01:36:35.583
to always rely on You.

794
01:36:37.625 --> 01:36:39.333
Strengthen my faith,

795
01:36:40.958 --> 01:36:42.333
for nothing

796
01:36:43.791 --> 01:36:46.750
would have meaning without Your presence, Father.

797
01:36:55.750 --> 01:36:57.250
We're two kilometers out.

798
01:37:00.375 --> 01:37:02.541
Hey, get my drone.

799
01:37:27.750 --> 01:37:29.208
Look at this.

800
01:37:29.291 --> 01:37:31.250
There's no need to send someone for recon.

801
01:37:31.333 --> 01:37:32.875
We can just use my drone.

802
01:37:55.958 --> 01:37:57.375
Shit.

803
01:38:04.333 --> 01:38:05.916
Fuck this guy!

804
01:38:08.125 --> 01:38:10.291
Okay, everybody in, get moving!

805
01:38:11.083 --> 01:38:12.000
Remember!

806
01:38:12.083 --> 01:38:14.166
Never underestimate your opponents!

807
01:38:14.958 --> 01:38:15.791
Got it?

808
01:38:22.666 --> 01:38:23.833
Do we go now, too?

809
01:38:25.541 --> 01:38:26.875
Later.

810
01:38:29.291 --> 01:38:31.291
Fuck! Bastard!

811
01:39:13.541 --> 01:39:15.125
Seriously?

812
01:39:15.208 --> 01:39:17.333
All of us just to go up against a family?

813
01:39:20.333 --> 01:39:21.583
Crazy.

814
01:39:21.666 --> 01:39:23.583
Maybe your boss is high.

815
01:40:51.041 --> 01:40:54.208
Lord, forgive us if we hurt those who have wronged us.

816
01:40:55.791 --> 01:40:57.708
This is self-defense, God.

817
01:42:30.041 --> 01:42:31.666
Shit. Putri!

818
01:42:33.166 --> 01:42:34.125
Grandpa!

819
01:42:34.791 --> 01:42:36.000
Grandpa!

820
01:42:36.083 --> 01:42:36.958
Dimas.

821
01:42:52.583 --> 01:42:54.000
Motherfucker!

822
01:42:59.416 --> 01:43:01.208
It's just self-defense, God!

823
01:43:06.875 --> 01:43:08.416
God, please help me!

824
01:43:16.125 --> 01:43:17.125
Son of a bitch!

825
01:43:19.125 --> 01:43:21.250
Putri! Grandpa! Help!

826
01:43:27.416 --> 01:43:28.666
Help!

827
01:43:48.250 --> 01:43:50.250
God, please point my arrow at that guy.

828
01:43:57.208 --> 01:43:59.333
Please! In Jesus' name!

829
01:44:03.666 --> 01:44:05.500
- Fuck! - Shit!

830
01:44:12.833 --> 01:44:16.083
Grandpa! Help!

831
01:44:17.375 --> 01:44:19.958
Grandpa! Grandpa!

832
01:44:25.666 --> 01:44:26.666
Hey!

833
01:45:14.916 --> 01:45:16.333
Get inside!

834
01:45:18.875 --> 01:45:20.083
Motherfucker!

835
01:45:25.583 --> 01:45:28.000
You son of a bitch!

836
01:45:28.083 --> 01:45:29.291
God, help!

837
01:45:29.375 --> 01:45:32.250
If I get out alive, I promise to be good.

838
01:45:32.333 --> 01:45:34.750
I won't hurt anyone ever again. God!

839
01:46:00.375 --> 01:46:01.458
Chicken…

840
01:46:06.708 --> 01:46:07.833
My God!

841
01:46:08.833 --> 01:46:10.833
God, forgive me. Amen.

842
01:47:22.666 --> 01:47:24.583
Ton. Kus.

843
01:47:25.750 --> 01:47:27.208
Report on positions.

844
01:47:37.125 --> 01:47:38.666
Who the hell is this guy?

845
01:47:39.541 --> 01:47:41.208
Ex-Special Forces.

846
01:47:42.541 --> 01:47:43.791
No way!

847
01:47:44.458 --> 01:47:46.833
You really should read your messages.

848
01:47:49.041 --> 01:47:50.875
I'm dyslexic, asshole.

849
01:48:12.291 --> 01:48:13.125
Geg!

850
01:48:20.458 --> 01:48:21.333
Do!

851
01:48:58.875 --> 01:49:00.208
Be careful.

852
01:49:49.416 --> 01:49:50.333
Dimas, hide!

853
01:50:49.375 --> 01:50:50.916
To the pond!

854
01:51:12.041 --> 01:51:13.708
Putri! Run!

855
01:51:56.666 --> 01:51:59.291
God, what do I do? Fuck.

856
01:52:11.208 --> 01:52:13.416
- Dimas, you okay? - I'm fine.

857
01:52:41.083 --> 01:52:42.416
Putri.

858
01:53:02.666 --> 01:53:03.833
Putri, hurry.

859
01:53:10.916 --> 01:53:12.416
Putri, what are you waiting for?

860
01:53:12.500 --> 01:53:14.250
Hold it, Dimas, he's in the way.

861
01:53:38.583 --> 01:53:39.416
Putri!

862
01:53:39.500 --> 01:53:41.166
Putri, hurry! Grandpa!

863
01:53:41.250 --> 01:53:42.291
Shush! Wait!

864
01:53:43.125 --> 01:53:44.958
Putri! Now!

865
01:53:45.041 --> 01:53:46.708
See? Do it!

866
01:53:47.291 --> 01:53:49.208
Putri! Trust me!

867
01:53:50.708 --> 01:53:51.541
Okay.

868
01:54:55.708 --> 01:54:57.375
- Grandpa! - Putri, run!

869
01:55:10.666 --> 01:55:12.875
Fuck you! Go to hell, all of you!

870
01:55:46.208 --> 01:55:48.875
- We have to save Grandpa. - Not yet, it's dangerous.

871
01:56:01.000 --> 01:56:02.291
I want to help too.

872
01:56:05.875 --> 01:56:08.375
But the other day, Grandpa taught me to be patient.

873
01:56:10.708 --> 01:56:13.958
If we're patient, we can think of a better plan to help him.

874
01:56:19.500 --> 01:56:20.500
Two more to go.

875
01:56:21.750 --> 01:56:22.916
There's two of us.

876
01:56:24.833 --> 01:56:26.250
And we have two arrows.

877
01:56:30.583 --> 01:56:31.916
And we have this.

878
01:57:00.833 --> 01:57:02.958
Before you go to meet my brother,

879
01:57:03.958 --> 01:57:05.750
hand over the data.

880
01:57:18.291 --> 01:57:21.125
Where is it?

881
01:57:28.000 --> 01:57:29.166
This son of a bitch.

882
01:57:32.583 --> 01:57:33.791
Let's find out.

883
01:57:36.458 --> 01:57:38.708
If we cut off his balls,

884
01:57:40.166 --> 01:57:41.916
will he make it?

885
01:57:42.000 --> 01:57:43.375
Let Grandpa go!

886
01:57:46.083 --> 01:57:47.916
Or we'll leak those files you want!

887
01:57:51.250 --> 01:57:52.875
Do, check it out.

888
01:57:54.875 --> 01:57:56.166
Motherfuckers.

889
01:58:02.375 --> 01:58:03.375
Kid!

890
01:58:13.083 --> 01:58:14.083
Kid!

891
01:58:21.166 --> 01:58:22.375
Where are you, kid?

892
01:58:28.166 --> 01:58:31.666
Stop! Take one step further and you'll get an arrow in your head!

893
01:58:38.875 --> 01:58:40.916
You're full of hot air, kid.

894
01:58:55.916 --> 01:58:57.291
Motherfucker!

895
01:58:57.916 --> 01:58:58.833
All good, Do?

896
01:58:58.916 --> 01:58:59.958
All good.

897
01:59:02.291 --> 01:59:04.541
Let Grandpa go! Untie him!

898
01:59:04.625 --> 01:59:06.333
I'll tell you where the files are!

899
01:59:22.083 --> 01:59:23.666
Your grandpa is free!

900
01:59:25.166 --> 01:59:26.750
Now, where are the files?

901
01:59:29.333 --> 01:59:30.833
Answer the question!

902
01:59:30.916 --> 01:59:32.458
Your grandpa is free!

903
01:59:43.666 --> 01:59:45.291
You little brat!

904
02:00:16.625 --> 02:00:17.791
Watch this!

905
02:00:18.875 --> 02:00:21.291
I'll kill your grandpa!

906
02:00:22.125 --> 02:00:23.541
Just like your father!

907
02:00:27.000 --> 02:00:29.541
This is for Bastian.

908
02:00:34.166 --> 02:00:35.083
Fuck!

909
02:00:40.833 --> 02:00:43.333
Motherfucker…

910
02:00:45.333 --> 02:00:46.500
Son of a bitch!

911
02:00:55.208 --> 02:00:56.791
Kid, you son of a bitch!

912
02:01:26.333 --> 02:01:27.750
I will make sure

913
02:01:28.625 --> 02:01:32.208
your grandkids are burnt to ashes,

914
02:01:32.291 --> 02:01:34.041
just like this house.

915
02:01:35.416 --> 02:01:36.291
Just burn it.

916
02:01:38.125 --> 02:01:40.083
I can rebuild it.

917
02:01:40.875 --> 02:01:41.833
Really?

918
02:01:52.041 --> 02:01:53.208
I'll make sure

919
02:01:53.958 --> 02:01:56.166
you die first.

920
02:05:02.708 --> 02:05:04.083
Time to die, kid.

921
02:06:35.708 --> 02:06:36.875
Dimas!

922
02:06:55.958 --> 02:06:56.875
Fuck you!

923
02:07:01.000 --> 02:07:02.625
What do you want, cunt?

924
02:07:13.541 --> 02:07:14.666
Putri!

925
02:07:22.500 --> 02:07:23.583
Dimas!

926
02:07:41.458 --> 02:07:42.458
Dimas…

927
02:07:42.541 --> 02:07:44.291
Dimas, are you okay?

928
02:07:44.375 --> 02:07:46.125
Are you okay?

929
02:09:06.375 --> 02:09:07.875
Motherfucker!

930
02:09:38.333 --> 02:09:40.083
Grandpa!

931
02:09:45.041 --> 02:09:47.000
- Grandpa! Wake up! - Grandpa!

932
02:09:47.625 --> 02:09:48.708
- Grandpa! - Grandpa!

933
02:09:49.208 --> 02:09:51.708
- Grandpa… - Grandpa!

934
02:09:51.791 --> 02:09:53.750
- Grandpa! - Grandpa!

935
02:09:56.541 --> 02:09:58.333
Not there, that hurts.

936
02:09:59.750 --> 02:10:00.750
Grandpa!

937
02:10:00.833 --> 02:10:01.875
Grandpa…

938
02:10:03.083 --> 02:10:04.208
Grandpa!

939
02:10:19.958 --> 02:10:21.541
- That hurts. - Okay.

940
02:10:23.291 --> 02:10:25.166
My rate is 10,000 per hour.

941
02:10:27.125 --> 02:10:28.916
Let me refill your drink.

942
02:10:29.000 --> 02:10:30.000
- Right. - Here you go.

943
02:10:33.333 --> 02:10:34.416
Grandpa.

944
02:10:34.500 --> 02:10:35.875
- Dimas, here. - Here you go.

945
02:10:35.958 --> 02:10:37.125
Dad's flash drive.

946
02:10:42.666 --> 02:10:43.833
What do you wanna do with it?

947
02:10:46.208 --> 02:10:47.208
We'll deal with it later.

948
02:10:50.666 --> 02:10:51.666
And now?

949
02:10:55.500 --> 02:10:57.416
Now we rebuild all this.

950
02:11:01.375 --> 02:11:03.000
Grandpa…

951
02:11:03.083 --> 02:11:05.833
If I live here, I don't need to go to school, right?

952
02:11:05.916 --> 02:11:08.125
You wish.

953
02:11:08.208 --> 02:11:09.125
Is that so wrong?

954
02:11:09.208 --> 02:11:10.833
- Are you sick of school? - I am!

955
02:11:27.041 --> 02:11:30.250
I've patched up all the leaks in Ulo's organization, sir.

956
02:11:31.666 --> 02:11:34.291
The problem is, that's not the only leak.

957
02:11:35.291 --> 02:11:37.375
If you're worried about that old man,

958
02:11:38.625 --> 02:11:39.833
he's not a problem.

959
02:11:41.791 --> 02:11:45.291
He won't do anything as long as his family's safe, sir.

960
02:11:46.083 --> 02:11:47.333
Just trust me.

961
02:11:48.541 --> 02:11:49.958
Are you sure?

962
02:11:51.208 --> 02:11:52.500
I can guarantee it, sir.

963
02:11:53.958 --> 02:11:55.875
He got justice anyway, right?

964
02:11:59.708 --> 02:12:02.083
It's best we focus on finding

965
02:12:03.083 --> 02:12:04.791
a replacement for Ulo now.

966
02:12:13.625 --> 02:12:14.666
Checkmate.

967
